## Boot flow (UI + background entrypoints)

### Startup entrypoints

- App startup: `src/Bible.Alarm/MauiProgram.cs`
- Bootstrap orchestration: `src/Bible.Alarm/Services/Bootstrap/BootstrapOrchestrator.cs`

Bootstrap can run:
- in the UI process (normal app launch)
- in a background process (Android Auto services, alarm receiver)

The orchestrator is protected by a semaphore and a static “already verified” flag, so it is safe to call multiple times.

### What bootstrap does (in order)

In `BootstrapOrchestrator.VerifyServicesAsync(initializeUi)`:
- runs in parallel:
  - `DatabaseBootstrapService.InitializeAsync()` (schedule DB migration + media migration)
  - `FluxorBootstrapService.InitializeAsync()` (store init)
  - `ResourceBootstrapService.CopyResourcesAsync()` (embedded resources)
- sends `InitializedMessage` early when `initializeUi=true` to show the Home page while schedule loading continues
- loads schedules into Fluxor state via `ScheduleBootstrapService.InitializeAsync()`
- runs platform bootstrap via `IPlatformBootstrapService.InitializeAsync()` (notification channels + background jobs)

