## Cascade logic (auto-populating selections)

The schedule editor uses **cascade handlers** so that selecting higher-level fields (category/language/publication/section) auto-selects the next valid fields.

If you’re working on this area, also read:
- `schedule-cascade-deep-dive.mdc` (full “how it really works”, including ad-hoc catalog + no-language publications + save persistence)

### Category cascade (category → language → publication → section → track)

- `src/Bible.Alarm/Stores/Effects/ScheduleEffectsHelpers/CategorySelectionAutoPopulateHandler.cs`

Key behaviors:
- tries to preserve previous language if it exists in the new category
- otherwise defaults to English `"E"` when available
- catalogs the chosen publication on-demand via `ILanguageContentService.EnsurePublicationExistsAsync(...)` when needed
- supports “no-language” publications (`LanguageId == null`) by selecting them without cataloging

### Bible cascade (language → publication → section → track)

- `src/Bible.Alarm/Stores/Effects/ScheduleEffectsHelpers/BiblePublicationCascadeHandler.cs`

Key behaviors:
- keeps user-selected publication when possible, and only falls back to a new one if it can’t be queried for that language
- uses PublicationLanguages + BiblePublications to choose a valid publication for the language
- supports “no-language” publications for some categories (notably Music)
- guards against infinite dispatch loops by comparing current vs computed values before dispatching

### Music cascade (music type → language → publication → section → track)

- `src/Bible.Alarm/Stores/Effects/ScheduleEffectsHelpers/MusicCascadeHandler.cs`

Key behaviors:
- for VocalMusic, defaults language to English `"E"`
- for Instrumental music, selects publications where `LanguageId == null`
- respects sectioned melody publications (e.g. discs) via `SectionCode`
- when switching music types, `ScheduleEffects` may populate missing `MusicSectionName` from the selected track (instrumental/no-language, sectioned publications):
  - `src/Bible.Alarm/Stores/Effects/ScheduleEffects.cs` → `PopulateMusicSectionNameForStateAsync(...)`

